# check-skills.allow — names in the skills that are legitimately not repo symbols.
# One per line, `#` comments. Keep this SHORT: every entry is a name the drift
# check can no longer protect, so an entry needs a reason that is not "it was
# easier". Format: a bare token, `tool.argument`, `test.method`, or a path.

# --- Tools belonging to OTHER MCP servers ---------------------------------
# The chrome-devtools MCP (declared in .mcp.json, not built here), named by
# game-browser-test and by the fallback snippets the relay tools print.
evaluate_script
take_screenshot
take_snapshot
handle_dialog
list_console_messages
list_network_requests
new_page
navigate_page
select_page
performance_start_trace
performance_stop_trace

# --- taskherd MCP (user-level server, ~/.claude.json) ----------------------
tasks_status
tasks_add
tasks_block
tasks_fork
tasks_note
tasks_ack
tasks_options
tasks_init

# --- Result strings and enum values, not identifiers ----------------------
